<title>UK: Russia's Komi region plans $200 mln five-year bond.</title>
<headline>Russia's Komi region plans $200 mln five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's northern Komi Republic plans to launch a $200 million five-year Eurobond by the end of the year, senior officials from the region told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We plan to raise $200 million by the end of the year,&quot; Komi minister of finance Alexander Zakharov said.  </p>
<p>Komi economy minister Anatoly Karakchiev said the maturity was likely to be five years.</p>
<p>No investment banks have yet won the mandate for the transaction, the ministers said.</p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
